        "original_id": "5760d435-195b-535e-abe6-5d8abb41b2f2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Luca Cordero di Montezemolo, Enzo Ferrari, Piero Ferrari, Jean Todt, Amedeo Felisa, Massimo Fumarola\n- Companies: Ferrari, Fiat S.p.A., Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV\n- Organizations: Confindustria, FIEG, Pininfarina, FerrariWorld\n- Products: Ferrari Ascari\n- Concepts: automotive industry, holding company merger\n\nFacts:\n- Luca Cordero di Montezemolo was born on 31 August 1947 and is an Italian businessman.\n- Luca Cordero di Montezemolo was formerly Chairman of Ferrari.\n- Luca Cordero di Montezemolo was formerly Chairman of Fiat S.p.A.\n- Luca Cordero di Montezemolo was President of Confindustria and FIEG.\n- Fiat S.p.A., \"Fabbrica Italiana Automobili Torino,\" was an Italian holding company whose original and core activities were in the automotive industry.\n- On 29 January 2014, Fiat S.p.A. announced that it would merge into the new Netherlands-based holding company Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV.\n- Before the end of 2014, Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV succeeded Fiat S.p.A.\n- In the Ferrari Ascari competition, the judges included Luca Cordero di Montezemolo, Piero Ferrari, Jean Todt, Amedeo Felisa, Massimo Fumarola, Pininfarina, and more than 22,000 FerrariWorld online users.\n- Piero Ferrari was identified as the second and only living son of Enzo Ferrari.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "067543a5-d207-5165-9562-b2a0b5df4193",
        "text": "Page: Luca Cordero di Montezemolo. Sentence: Luca Cordero di Montezemolo (] ; born 31 August 1947) is an Italian businessman, former Chairman of Ferrari, and formerly Chairman of Fiat S.p.A. and President of Confindustria and FIEG.\nPage: Fiat S.p.A.. Sentence: Fiat S.p.A., or \"Fabbrica Italiana Automobili Torino\" (Italian Automobile Factory of Turin), was an Italian holding company whose original and core activities were in the automotive industry, and that was succeeded by Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV (FCA).\nPage: Fiat S.p.A.. Sentence: On 29 January 2014, it was announced that Fiat S.p.A. (the former owner of Fiat Group) was to be merged into a new Netherlands-based holding company Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV (FCA), took place before the end of 2014.\nPage: Ferrari Ascari. Sentence: The judges of the competition included Luca Cordero di Montezemolo, the second and only living son of Enzo Ferrari, Piero Ferrari, Jean Todt, Amedeo Felisa, Massimo Fumarola, Pininfarina, and more than 22,000 users of FerrariWorld's online website.",
